### Journey C — Failed premium recovery

1. Collection attempt fails.
2. Payment failure is recorded.
3. Insurer receives the payment result.
4. Customer receives an appropriate notification.
5. Eligible recovery action is initiated.
6. Subsequent payment result is reconciled against the original premium obligation.
7. Insurer applies the relevant policy and grace-period rules.
8. Unrecovered obligations are escalated according to insurer policy.

A retry is a new payment attempt against the relevant billing obligation, not a new policy or a new premium obligation.

## 8. Grace period, lapse, and reinstatement

Insurance collection requires a clear distinction between payment status and policy status.

| Concept | Meaning | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| Premium due | Premium obligation has reached its due date | Insurer / billing source |
| Payment pending | Collection result is not final | Payment flow |
| Payment failed | Collection attempt was unsuccessful | Payment flow |
| Outstanding premium | Premium remains unpaid | Insurer |
| Grace period | Contractual period defined by insurer | Insurer |
| Lapsed policy | Policy status changed under policy terms | Insurer |
| Reinstatement | Policy restored under insurer rules | Insurer |

### Example timeline

Illustrative only:

```text
